        "titulo": "The plural: cinco jeitos",
        "explicacao": "The German plural is formed in five ways: -e (der Tisch → die Tische), -(e)n (die Lampe → die Lampen), -er (das Buch → die Bücher), no ending (der Lehrer → die Lehrer) and -s (das Auto → die Autos, common in foreign words). Many words also take an umlaut on the vowel (a → ä, o → ö, u → ü), a bit like English «foot → feet» or «mouse → mice». There is no safe rule: learn the plural together with the noun. The definite article of the plural is always «die», for all three genders.",
        "comparacao": "The English plural is almost always just «-s» (apart from a few oddities like «children»). The German plural has five forms, and you have to memorise them with each word.",
